      "notes": "Bold fanfare shape -- a wide leap up, settle, breathe -- built for horns, not voice. Short and punchy (1 bar) on purpose, contrast to the last piece's long legato line."
    },
    "notes": "Horn-driven jazz-rock in the vein of 70s brass-rock bands: driving rock rhythm section underneath, sophisticated horn-chart harmony on top. voicing='drop2' throughout -- unlike the funk piece's tight 'closed' stabs or the ballad's spread 'open' pads, drop2 (second-from-top voice dropped an octave) is the actual technique horn arrangers use for a big-but-still-punchy brass sound. Structure escalates harmonically on purpose: intro_riff and verse stay mostly plain triads/7ths (rock-song simplicity), horn_hook loads in 9ths/13ths/an altered dominant for the big brass chorus, outro_vamp closes on repeated dominant-tonic stabs. groove='push' on the hook section specifically, for that leaning-into-the-beat horn-band urgency; 'driving' elsewhere.",
